course: dictionary
lesson: 6750
title: Onondaga: keepers of the central fire
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Onondaga starts with a capital letter because it is a name. A name can belong to a people, a language or a place. Read the words around it to find out which one. «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca, later the Tuscarora, under a Great Law of Peace.» Onondaga sits in a list of peoples, so it names a people.
explain: The clues also tell you what the people did. The Onondaga are known as the keepers of the central fire, the place where the Grand Council of chiefs meets. Keepers means they look after something important. The Great Law of Peace is linked with them too.
explain: Onondaga can also name a place. Onondaga Lake and Onondaga County are near Syracuse, New York. When Onondaga comes before lake or county, think of a place. Always ask: who or what is this? Then check the clues around the word.
fact: Onondaga is a noun for a Native American people of central New York State.
fact: The Onondaga are one of the Six Nations of the Haudenosaunee, also called the Iroquois Confederacy.
fact: Onondaga is also the name of their language.
fact: Onondaga is a name for a lake and a county near Syracuse, New York.
fact: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca, later the Tuscarora, under a Great Law of Peace.»
exercise: In «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca», find and copy one word that names a people. | *Onondaga | Peace | Great | Confederacy
exercise: «Onondaga Lake lies near Syracuse, New York.» What kind of word is Onondaga in that sentence? | A type of bird | A number | A verb meaning to swim | *A place name
exercise: The Onondaga are called keepers of the central fire. What does keepers mean here? | People who run away from fires | *People who look after something important | A type of fire engine | People who sell fire wood
test: Which group were the Onondaga one of? | The Gold Coast | *The Six Nations of the Haudenosaunee | The Seven Seas | The Roman Empire
test: Onondaga Lake is near which city? | Boston | *Syracuse, New York | Chicago
exam: Why are the Onondaga called keepers of the central fire? | Because they live by the sea | Because they keep bees at the lake | Because they sell fire engines | *Because the Grand Council of chiefs meets at their central fire
